<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>ACL Components Pte Ltd — Design Change Request Insights</title>
<style>
  .viz-root {
    color-scheme: light;
    --surface-1:      #fcfcfb;
    --page-plane:     #f9f9f7;
    --text-primary:   #0b0b0b;
    --text-secondary: #52514e;
    --text-muted:     #898781;
    --gridline:       #e1e0d9;
    --baseline:       #c3c2b7;
    --border:         rgba(11,11,11,0.10);
    --success-text:   #2f6b34;

    --series-1: #1D6693; /* muted blue   - Admin */
    --series-2: #C2703D; /* muted clay   - Examiner */
    --series-3: #0E8E78; /* muted teal   - Approver */
    --series-4: #B8862B; /* muted gold   - QA Approver */

    --seq-100: #D6E4EE; --seq-200: #AFC9DC; --seq-300: #86AFC9; --seq-400: #5C93B3; --seq-500: #1D6693;

    --good: #4F8F55;
    --warning: #C79A3E;
    --serious: #C15C5C;
    --critical: #A83E3E;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:where(:not([data-theme="light"])) .viz-root {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --surface-1:      #1a1a19;
      --page-plane:     #0d0d0d;
      --text-primary:   #ffffff;
      --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;
      --text-muted:     #898781;
      --gridline:       #2c2c2a;
      --baseline:       #383835;
      --border:         rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
      --success-text:   #8ec793;

      --series-1: #4C8FC4;
      --series-2: #C97D4C;
      --series-3: #2F9C83;
      --series-4: #B08429;

      --seq-100: #1F3A52; --seq-200: #2E5678; --seq-300: #3E7299; --seq-400: #4C8FC4; --seq-500: #7BB3DE;

      --good: #6BAF71;
      --warning: #D9B65C;
      --serious: #D67F7F;
      --critical: #D96A6A;
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"] .viz-root {
    color-scheme: dark;
    --surface-1:      #1a1a19;
    --page-plane:     #0d0d0d;
    --text-primary:   #ffffff;
    --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;
    --text-muted:     #898781;
    --gridline:       #2c2c2a;
    --baseline:       #383835;
    --border:         rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
    --success-text:   #8ec793;

    --series-1: #4C8FC4;
    --series-2: #C97D4C;
    --series-3: #2F9C83;
    --series-4: #B08429;

    --seq-100: #1F3A52; --seq-200: #2E5678; --seq-300: #3E7299; --seq-400: #4C8FC4; --seq-500: #7BB3DE;

    --good: #6BAF71;
    --warning: #D9B65C;
    --serious: #D67F7F;
    --critical: #D96A6A;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body {
    margin: 0; padding: 0;
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    background: var(--page-plane);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .viz-root { background: var(--page-plane); color: var(--text-primary); }

  .wrap { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 24px 80px; }

  header.page-head { margin-bottom: 32px; }
  header.page-head h1 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 6px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  header.page-head .subtitle { font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  header.page-head .meta { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.5; }

  .theme-toggle {
    position: fixed; top: 16px; right: 16px; z-index: 50;
    font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary);
    background: var(--surface-1); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 12px; cursor: pointer; user-select: none;
  }

  section.dcr-section { margin: 0 0 52px; padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--gridline); }
  section.dcr-section:first-of-type { border-top: none; padding-top: 0; }

  h2.section-title { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 6px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  p.section-sub { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0 0 20px; max-width: 760px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .note { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 10px 0 0; line-height: 1.5; }

  /* ---- Highlights grid ---- */
  .highlights { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .highlights { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .hl-card { background: var(--surface-1); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 14px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .hl-card::before { content: ""; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px; background: var(--accent); }
  .hl-card.good { --accent: var(--good); }
  .hl-card.warning { --accent: var(--warning); }
  .hl-card.critical { --accent: var(--critical); }
  .hl-rank { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .hl-value { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; margin-bottom: 4px; font-variant-numeric: proportional-nums; }
  .hl-value .unit { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .hl-label { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .hl-desc { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.45; }

  /* ---- Evidence / action boxes ---- */
  .evidence-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-top: 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .evidence-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .ebox { background: var(--surface-1); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; border-left: 3px solid var(--text-muted); }
  .ebox.action { border-left-color: var(--series-1); }
  .ebox .eb-label { font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .ebox.action .eb-label { color: var(--series-1); }
  .ebox p { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; }
  .ebox p b { color: var(--text-primary); }

  /* ---- big stat callout ---- */
  .stat-row { display: flex; gap: 32px; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .stat-big { font-size: 46px; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .stat-big .unit { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-left: 2px; }
  .stat-sub { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 620px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .stat-big.good { color: var(--good); }
  .stat-big.critical { color: var(--critical); }
  .stat-big.warning { color: #8a6100; }
  :root[data-theme="dark"] .stat-big.warning, @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .stat-big.warning { color: var(--warning); } }

  /* ---- concern callout ---- */
  .concern-card { background: var(--surface-1); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--critical); border-radius: 10px; padding: 20px 22px; }
  .concern-card .cc-tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--critical); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .concern-card p { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .concern-card p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .concern-card b { color: var(--text-primary); }

  /* ---- Bar chart (horizontal) ---- */
  .barchart { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .bar-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 168px 1fr 62px; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
  .bar-row .bar-label { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-primary); text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .bar-track { position: relative; height: 20px; background: transparent; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gridline); }
  .bar-fill { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 2px; height: 16px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--bar-color, var(--series-1)); transition: width .2s ease; }
  .bar-row .bar-value { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .bar-fill[title]:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); cursor: default; }
  .barchart.narrow .bar-row { grid-template-columns: 190px 1fr 68px; }
  .barchart.narrow .bar-label { white-space: normal; overflow: visible; text-overflow: unset; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.3; }

  /* ---- Split bar (rejected vs cancelled, stacked by type) ---- */
  .split-bar-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 190px 1fr 100px; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .split-bar-row:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .split-label { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-primary); text-align: right; line-height: 1.3; }
  .split-track { position: relative; height: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gridline); display: flex; align-items: flex-start; }
  .split-seg { height: 16px; margin-top: 2px; }
  .split-seg.rejected { background: var(--critical); border-radius: 4px 0 0 4px; }
  .split-seg.cancelled { background: var(--text-muted); border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0; margin-left: 2px; }
  .split-seg[title]:hover { filter: brightness(1.12); cursor: default; }
  .split-value { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .split-value .sv-total { display: block; }
  .split-value .sv-detail { display: block; font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 2px; }

  /* ---- Role-grouped reason breakdown ---- */
  .role-reason-group { margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .role-reason-group:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .rr-role-label { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 7px; }
  .rr-role-label .rr-role-count { font-weight: 500; color: var(--text-muted); margin-left: 4px; }

  /* ---- Lollipop variant (rate/percentage metrics) ---- */
  .lollipop-line { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 9px; height: 2px; border-radius: 1px; background: var(--bar-color, var(--series-1)); }
  .lollipop-dot { position: absolute; top: 4px; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); background: var(--bar-color, var(--series-1)); border: 2px solid var(--surface-1); cursor: default; }
  .lollipop-dot:hover { filter: brightness(1.12); }

  /* legend (kept for other sections/reference) */
  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; margin: 14px 0 4px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .legend-item { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .legend-swatch { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; display: inline-block; }

  /* grouped workload chart */
  .workload-person { margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .workload-person .wp-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .workload-person .wp-head .name { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; }
  .workload-person .wp-head .total { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .wp-bars { display: flex; height: 22px; border-radius: 5px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .wp-seg { height: 100%; position: relative; }
  .wp-seg:not(:last-child) { border-right: 2px solid var(--surface-1); }
  .wp-seg[title]:hover { filter: brightness(1.1); }

  /* ---- Donut chart ---- */
  .donut-wrap { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .donut-center-label { text-align: center; }
  .donut-center-label .dc-num { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 800; }
  .donut-center-label .dc-unit { font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-secondary); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .donut-legend { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; font-size: 13px; }
  .donut-legend .dl-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .donut-legend .dl-swatch { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 3px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .donut-legend .dl-name { color: var(--text-primary); min-width: 150px; }
  .donut-legend .dl-val { color: var(--text-secondary); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; margin-left: auto; }

  /* ---- Tornado (diverging) chart ---- */
  .tornado-head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 90px 1fr; font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .tornado-head .th-left { text-align: right; }
  .tornado-head .th-right { text-align: left; }
  .tornado-head .th-mid { text-align: center; }
  .tornado-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 90px 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .tornado-left { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .tornado-right { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .tornado-bar { height: 16px; }
  .tornado-left .tornado-bar { border-radius: 4px 0 0 4px; }
  .tornado-right .tornado-bar { border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0; }
  .tornado-mid { text-align: center; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; border-left: 1px solid var(--gridline); border-right: 1px solid var(--gridline); padding: 0 4px; }
  .tornado-val { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }

  /* ---- Gauge (radial) ---- */
  .gauge-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, max-content); gap: 20px 28px; }
  .gauge-item { text-align: center; }
  .gauge-item svg { display: block; }
  .gauge-label { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 6px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .gauge-sub { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--text-muted); }

  /* ---- Line chart ---- */
  .linechart-wrap svg { width: 100%; height: auto; }

  .grid-2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .grid-2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .grid-3 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) { .grid-3 { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .grid-3 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* ---- Recommendations ---- */
  .reco-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .reco-item { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr; gap: 14px; background: var(--surface-1); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  .reco-num { width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--series-1); color: #fff; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  .reco-item.priority .reco-num { background: var(--critical); }
  .reco-title { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .reco-body { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55; }
  .reco-body b { color: var(--text-primary); }

  footer.page-foot { margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--gridline); font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="viz-root" id="vizRoot">
  <button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle" type="button">🌓 Toggle theme</button>
  <div class="wrap">

    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>ACL Components Pte Ltd — Design Change Request Insights</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Design Change Request (DCR) approval pipeline &nbsp;·&nbsp; Data as of 2026-08-12</p>
      <p class="meta">Organized by theme — pipeline health, workload, risk drivers, timing, and trend — each section pairs the analysis and insight behind the numbers with a concrete next step.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Top 5 Highlights -->
    <section class="dcr-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Top 5 Highlights</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">The headline signals from the current 198-entry dataset — what's healthy, what's worth watching, and what needs a fix right now.</p>
      <div class="highlights">
        <div class="hl-card good">
          <div class="hl-rank">#1 · Health</div>
          <div class="hl-value">58.6<span class="unit">%</span></div>
          <div class="hl-label">Closed (116 of 198)</div>
          <div class="hl-desc">Well over half of all requests have completed the full four-stage approval chain end to end.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="hl-card warning">
          <div class="hl-rank">#2 · Attrition</div>
          <div class="hl-value">23.2<span class="unit">%</span></div>
          <div class="hl-label">Rejected + cancelled (46 of 198)</div>
          <div class="hl-desc">29 rejected, 17 cancelled. Up from 20.3% earlier in the dataset — worth tracking as a trend, not just a snapshot.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="hl-card critical">
          <div class="hl-rank">#3 · Bottleneck</div>
          <div class="hl-value">15<span class="unit">&nbsp;open</span></div>
          <div class="hl-label">Sitting at Pending Examiner</div>
          <div class="hl-desc">41.7% of all 36 currently-open requests (15 of 36) are stuck at one single stage.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="hl-card warning">
          <div class="hl-rank">#4 · Category risk</div>
          <div class="hl-value">32.0<span class="unit">%</span></div>
          <div class="hl-label">Electronics, PCB & Sensors non-completion</div>
          <div class="hl-desc">Highest failure rate of any category on a meaningful sample (8 of 25) — this one is a real action-item, not just a watch-item.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="hl-card critical">
          <div class="hl-rank">#5 · Overdue</div>
          <div class="hl-value">2<span class="unit">&nbsp;entries</span></div>
          <div class="hl-label">39 and 1 days past due</div>
          <div class="hl-desc">Both currently sit with Tan — one at Examiner (39 days), one at Admin (1 day) — the same person flagged in the bottleneck above.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Right now callout -->
    <section class="dcr-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Right Now: What Needs Attention</h2>
      <div class="concern-card">
        <div class="cc-tag">Concentrated, currently-active risk</div>
        <p>The Examiner stage is the largest bottleneck in the pipeline — <b>15 of 36 open requests (41.7%)</b> are stuck there. Within that queue, it isn't evenly spread: <b>Tan personally holds 6 of those 15 (40.0%)</b> — the most of any reviewer. Tan is also the reviewer of record on <b>both</b> of the module's currently-overdue items, one at Examiner (39 days) and one at Admin (1 day).</p>
        <p>No other single person or stage combination carries this much concentrated, active exposure right now. If Tan is out or falls further behind, the largest queue in the whole pipeline has no backup.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="evidence-grid">
        <div class="ebox">
          <div class="eb-label">Analysis and Insights</div>
          <p>The bottleneck and the overdue items aren't two separate problems — they're the same one. Both of the overdue requests and the Examiner-stage backlog sit with Tan, and Tan is carrying 40.0% of the current open Examiner queue against a 30.1% historical share of Examiner-stage work — meaningfully overloaded relative to his usual pace, not just unlucky timing. Fixing the queue distribution is very likely what clears the overdue items too, rather than these needing two separate fixes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ebox action">
          <div class="eb-label">Actionable Items</div>
          <p>Rebalance part of Tan's Examiner queue to Rose or Lim now, before the 2 overdue items become more, and confirm Tan isn't blocked on something upstream that's causing the backlog.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How the review process works -->
    <section class="dcr-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">How the Review Process Actually Works</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Before drilling into any one number, the shape of the workflow itself: how many times a request gets reviewed, and whether a rejection is ever revisited.</p>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div>
          <div class="stat-row"><div class="stat-big">1<span class="unit">pass · 4 stages</span></div></div>
          <p class="stat-sub">Admin → Examiner → Approver → QA Approver, in that order, exactly once. There is no "round 2" built into this workflow — a request either keeps moving forward or it terminates.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="stat-row"><div class="stat-big critical">29<span class="unit">of 198 rejected</span></div></div>
          <p class="stat-sub">Once any stage rejects a request, it stays Rejected for good — there is no in-place revision path back to Pending Admin.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="stat-row"><div class="stat-big good">10<span class="unit">of 29 resubmitted</span></div></div>
          <p class="stat-sub">10 of the 29 rejected requests were recreated as a brand-new DCR and linked back via the Resubmit For field — giving that design change a second full review cycle. Every one of those second-round reviews went on to close successfully.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="evidence-grid">
        <div class="ebox">
          <div class="eb-label">Analysis and Insights</div>
          <p>Every one of the 198 requests follows the same fixed 4-stage sequence with no revision loop back to an earlier stage — a rejected entry stays Rejected for good. That said, 10 of the 29 rejected requests (34.5%) were recreated as a brand-new DCR and given a second review cycle, and every one of those second-round reviews went on to close successfully. Reject reasons are now tracked by role too (see "Rejections by Stage &amp; Root Cause"), and they confirm why a full restart is the only option: Admin's rejections are pure paperwork gaps, while Examiner's and Approver's are genuine technical findings — neither can be patched in place under this workflow, only resolved and resubmitted from scratch.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ebox action">
          <div class="eb-label">Actionable Items</div>
          <p>Because there's no partial-redo path — a rejected request can only be fixed by resubmitting a brand-new DCR from scratch — preventing the rejection in the first place is worth far more than any fix on the back end. Three levers now stand out: a mandatory-fields check at submission would eliminate Admin's 9 paperwork-gap rejections outright (see "Rejections by Stage &amp; Root Cause"), intake triage on high-risk Request Reasons would catch Examiner-level issues earlier (see "Does the Stated Reason Predict Rejection?"), and a design review checklist for Electronics, PCB &amp; Sensors and Structural, Housing &amp; Mounting would target the riskiest categories (see "Category Volume &amp; Category Risk").</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pipeline / Workflow State -->
    <section class="dcr-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Pipeline &amp; Workflow State</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Where all 198 entries currently sit. The inner ring shows the terminal outcomes; the full ring shows every state including work still in progress.</p>
      <div class="donut-wrap">
        <div id="pipelineDonut"></div>
        <div class="donut-legend" id="pipelineLegend"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="evidence-grid">
        <div class="ebox">
